WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.069
Cedar Vale signs up for three years of

00:00:02.069 --> 00:00:02.667
service.

00:00:02.917 --> 00:00:05.614
The price is agreed from the start: twelve

00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:07.864
thousand dollars in year one, thirteen

00:00:07.864 --> 00:00:10.039
thousand two hundred in year two, and

00:00:10.039 --> 00:00:12.264
fourteen thousand five hundred and twenty in

00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:12.858
year three.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.368
How should HubSpot represent that?

00:00:15.618 --> 00:00:17.983
Start with the source agreement, its dated

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.158
price schedule and the billing arrangement

00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:21.378
you intend to use.

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:24.051
Each anniversary moves to the next agreed

00:00:24.051 --> 00:00:24.529
price;

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:27.381
it is not automatically a new sale or

00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:28.769
a renewal negotiation.

00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:31.835
In this fictional example, the commitment

00:00:31.835 --> 00:00:34.235
runs from January twenty twenty-seven

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:35.876
through December twenty twenty-nine.

00:00:36.126 --> 00:00:38.451
Each price applies for exactly one year.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.470
The total across the three years is thirty-nine

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.779
thousand seven hundred and twenty dollars.

00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:46.377
The contract term tells us how long the

00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:47.356
commitment lasts.

00:00:47.606 --> 00:00:50.050
The price schedule tells us which rate applies

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:50.422
when.

00:00:50.672 --> 00:00:52.698
Billing frequency answers a separate

00:00:52.698 --> 00:00:55.344
question: how often do we issue an invoice?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.473
With annual billing, the example has one

00:00:58.473 --> 00:01:00.698
charge of twelve thousand dollars in year

00:01:00.698 --> 00:01:03.498
one, then thirteen thousand two hundred,

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:05.398
then fourteen thousand five hundred and

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:05.856
twenty.

00:01:06.106 --> 00:01:08.729
Invoice issue and due dates still follow the

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:09.946
agreed billing terms.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.073
With monthly billing, year one has twelve

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.845
charges of one thousand dollars.

00:01:15.095 --> 00:01:17.357
Year two has twelve of eleven hundred.

00:01:17.607 --> 00:01:19.604
Year three has twelve of twelve hundred and

00:01:19.604 --> 00:01:19.996
ten.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.376
Both patterns cover the same three-year

00:01:22.376 --> 00:01:23.254
price schedule.

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:26.027
Keep the source agreement and its price

00:01:26.027 --> 00:01:27.475
schedule identifiable.

00:01:27.725 --> 00:01:29.919
The commercial Contract represents the

00:01:29.919 --> 00:01:31.223
commitment being managed.

00:01:31.473 --> 00:01:34.175
The Deal records the sales opportunity, and a

00:01:34.175 --> 00:01:36.325
Quote presents the proposal when that route

00:01:36.325 --> 00:01:36.956
is used.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:40.127
Represent each period with its own start,

00:01:40.127 --> 00:01:42.817
finite term, quantity and applicable price.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.945
The three phases are sequential.

00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:47.767
If all three prices start together, you have

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:50.167
described concurrent charges instead of a

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.232
yearly increase.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.994
Keep the full commitment separate from the

00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:55.121
current period's rate.

00:01:55.371 --> 00:01:57.465
Thirty-nine thousand seven hundred and

00:01:57.465 --> 00:01:59.830
twenty dollars is the three-year total.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.403
It is not this year's recurring rate or

00:02:02.403 --> 00:02:04.027
evidence of cash collected.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.244
HubSpot now documents ramp pricing in

00:02:07.244 --> 00:02:09.769
Revenue Hub quotes: add the product as

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:12.569
separate line items, set each phase's billing

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:15.219
start date, and give each phase its intended

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:15.644
term.

00:02:15.894 --> 00:02:18.767
This is a documented option, not a completed

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.011
setup demonstration.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.718
That quote route requires Revenue Hub

00:02:22.718 --> 00:02:25.443
Professional or Enterprise and a Revenue Hub

00:02:25.443 --> 00:02:25.829
seat.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.727
The documentation also states a restriction

00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:31.285
on ramp pricing with HubSpot payments.

00:02:31.535 --> 00:02:34.357
Verify the processor and account path before

00:02:34.357 --> 00:02:35.865
promising automated billing.

00:02:36.533 --> 00:02:39.106
A direct Contract and a billing migration are

00:02:39.106 --> 00:02:40.416
separate setup routes.

00:02:40.666 --> 00:02:42.814
Check which one your account supports and

00:02:42.814 --> 00:02:44.762
how it handles dated line items.

00:02:45.012 --> 00:02:47.960
A migration ramp key belongs to its migration

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.553
process;

00:02:48.803 --> 00:02:51.022
it is not a field every quote needs.

00:02:51.272 --> 00:02:53.420
Choose the route before copying the schedule

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.344
into HubSpot.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.673
If Finance bills elsewhere, keep that system

00:02:57.673 --> 00:03:00.323
responsible for its invoice schedule and check

00:03:00.323 --> 00:03:00.995
the handoff.

00:03:01.245 --> 00:03:04.242
Recording three prices in HubSpot alone does

00:03:04.242 --> 00:03:06.407
not configure the external billing system.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.520
Now test the boundary, not just the total.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.493
On December thirty-first, twenty

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:14.399
twenty-seven, the example is still in year one.

00:03:14.649 --> 00:03:17.343
From January first, twenty twenty-eight, year

00:03:17.343 --> 00:03:18.575
two's price applies.

00:03:18.825 --> 00:03:20.972
There should be no overlap and no missing

00:03:20.972 --> 00:03:21.918
service period.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.144
For the monthly pattern, the expected rate

00:03:25.144 --> 00:03:27.219
changes from one thousand to eleven

00:03:27.219 --> 00:03:28.040
hundred dollars.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.234
The old phase must stop before the new

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.085
one charges.

00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:33.061
Adding both would produce twenty-one

00:03:33.061 --> 00:03:35.004
hundred dollars for the same month.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.114
Repeat the check at the next anniversary,

00:03:38.114 --> 00:03:39.864
when the monthly rate becomes twelve

00:03:39.864 --> 00:03:41.171
hundred and ten dollars.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.840
For annual billing, check the corresponding

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.218
annual amount instead.

00:03:45.468 --> 00:03:48.616
These are expected results; no invoices or

00:03:48.616 --> 00:03:51.057
automatic transitions were executed here.

00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:53.856
At the end of year three, confirm what

00:03:53.856 --> 00:03:55.424
the agreement actually says.

00:03:55.674 --> 00:03:58.325
Do not invent a fourth-year price or assume

00:03:58.325 --> 00:03:59.386
automatic renewal.

00:03:59.636 --> 00:04:01.980
Keep the source terms, commercial records

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.476
and billing schedule aligned.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.011
Reconcile the complete schedule.

00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:08.755
Twelve thousand, plus thirteen thousand two

00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:11.380
hundred, plus fourteen thousand five hundred

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:14.080
and twenty equals thirty-nine thousand seven

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.455
hundred and twenty dollars.

00:04:15.705 --> 00:04:18.578
Thirty-six monthly charges produce the same

00:04:18.578 --> 00:04:21.053
total before taxes and other agreed

00:04:21.053 --> 00:04:21.721
adjustments.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.719
Here's one row to record in the companion

00:04:24.719 --> 00:04:25.259
workbook.

00:04:25.509 --> 00:04:28.081
The boundary is the first of January, twenty

00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:28.709
twenty-eight.

00:04:28.959 --> 00:04:31.803
For monthly billing, the expected active rate

00:04:31.803 --> 00:04:34.278
is eleven hundred dollars, with the old

00:04:34.278 --> 00:04:36.212
one-thousand-dollar phase ended.

00:04:36.462 --> 00:04:38.766
Finance checks the actual billing result;

00:04:39.016 --> 00:04:41.560
Sales Ops records the source schedule and

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.600
any discrepancy.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.373
Leave the observed result open until you've

00:04:45.373 --> 00:04:45.986
tested it.

00:04:46.236 --> 00:04:49.205
If both phases charge, correct the overlap

00:04:49.205 --> 00:04:51.180
and repeat the check before activating the

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:51.783
schedule.

00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:54.177
The companion pack gives you the

00:04:54.177 --> 00:04:56.902
phased-pricing worksheet, configuration

00:04:56.902 --> 00:04:59.452
decision checklist and transition tests.

00:04:59.702 --> 00:05:02.700
Map one real agreement, name the owner,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.200
compare expected and observed results, and

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.553
resolve discrepancies before automating.
